Year = {2015},
Volume = {116},
Pages = {1-10},
Month = {MAY},
Abstract = {Using the newly developed Middle East Dust Index (MEDI) applied to MODIS
   satellite data, we consider a relationship between the recent
   desertified regions, over the past three decades, and the dust source
   points identified during the period of 2001-2012. Results indicate that
   major source points are located in Iraq and Syria, and by implementing
   the spectral mixture analysis on the Landsat TM images (1984 and 2012),
   a novel desertification map was extracted. Results of this study
   indicate for the first time that c.a., 39\% of all detected source
   points are located in this newly anthropogenically desertified area
   Using extracted indices for Deep Blue algorithm, dust sources were
   classified into three levels of intensity: low, medium, and high. A
   large number of low frequency sources are located within or close to the
   newly desertified areas. These severely desertified regions require
   immediate concern at a global scale. (C) 2015 Elsevier Ltd. All rights
   reserved.},
